  "edge_schema": "voltmarkt_edge_pat",
  "prompt": "Days just before a promotion can be unusual, so Pricing also compares each promotion with the same calendar days a year earlier. For each promotion that started in 2025 (start_date from 1 January to 31 December 2025), take the units sold on promotion, and the units its products sold from start_date moved back one year to end_date moved back one year, both days included, whatever promotion those lines carry. A line counts for a promotion when it carries it in order_lines.promo_id, and every such line falls within the promotion's dates; where two promotions overlap on a product, a line carries only the deeper one, so it counts once. Days are sales.order_date, the UTC day of the order. A period with no sale counts 0 units. Give uplift_units, this year's units minus last year's, and uplift_pct, that difference as a percentage of last year's units, rounded to 1 decimal with ROUND (12.5 for 12.5%), or missing when last year's units are 0. Return three columns, in this order: promo_id, uplift_units and uplift_pct. Return one row for each such promotion. Any row order is fine.",
  "output_contract": {
    "columns": [
      {
        "name": "promo_id",
        "type_class": "numeric"
      },
      {
        "name": "uplift_units",
        "type_class": "numeric"
      },
      {
        "name": "uplift_pct",
        "type_class": "numeric"
      }
    ],
    "grain": null
  },
